     "description": "Retired. It asked where each point stood in relation to the study area and passed every one of them on, labelled; `clip_points_to_area` asks the same question and acts on the answer, and a map draws inside and outside without being asked. Two widgets had grown into the question this one existed to answer, so it was answering nothing on its own. The practitioner, 2026-10-21, closing admission criterion D2: \"Let's retire coverage check.\" A saved node migrates to `clip_points_to_area`, stamped, and an edge into a map's `coverage` port becomes an ordinary `points` edge. The Spatial coverage exercise it was built around keeps its four records -- inside, on the boundary, outside, and one with no location -- and now demonstrates the clip.",
