  "fill_interior_gaps": {
   "version": "0.1.0",
   "released": "2026-10-10",
   "changes": [
    {
     "kind": "initial",
     "description": "Each polygon replaced by its outer ring, so enclosed gaps become solid. This is isochrone's fillHoles as a step of its own, and it is what Advanced-1 NB03 does: Polygon(new_iso.exterior) at cell 64, the definition that produced the shapefiles NB04 reads. Cell 94 redefines the function to take a convex hull of multipart results and never calls it, which had earlier been mistaken for the operative infill. Takes no UTM zone, unlike the nine widgets that do: the input states the metric CRS its upstream used and this reads it, because a zone asked for twice can be answered twice. Gaps between separate polygons are untouched -- it fills enclosed space and does not join things up. The dangerous case governs itself through the port type: donut_geomask, where a hole is the privacy mechanism, emits points and cannot reach a polygons input. See docs/experiments/88-filling-interior-gaps.md."
    }
   ],
   "breaking": false,
   "migrationFrom": []
  },
  "find_health_facilities": {
   "version": "0.5.0",
   "released": "2026-11-24",
   "changes": [
    {
     "kind": "changed",
     "description": "THE INSPECTOR IS ON THE STANDARD. Settings holds Configure... alone and primary, as every other standard step's does; Retrieve facilities -- or Fetch the registers -- moves to Result, beside what it produces, and is primary until there is something and again when what is held is not what the settings now ask for. The two shared one row before, with the emphasis moving between them by state, so the one thing to do next was whichever the markup had decided. The retrieval is a different kind of act from Configure...: it reaches the network and changes what the step holds, where Configure... only opens a dialog."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fixed",
     "description": "The Configure... dialog told the reader to retrieve \"under Settings\", which is not where the button is. It names Result now, and says to apply the settings first. The matching dialog and the refusal raised when no register has been fetched said the same wrong place and now say the right one."
    }
   ],
