     "description": "A layer of lines already drawn reopened showing the whole world. `fitBounds` ran synchronously at mount, when the dialog's panel still had no size, so it fitted the lines into a viewport of 0 x 0 and chose a zoom for that; the `invalidateSize` added the same day corrected the SIZE afterwards and nothing re-fitted. That first fix settled the tiles and not the view, which is why the basemap came back and the lines stayed a world away. The fit now waits for the first moment the container has width and height, and happens ONCE: re-fitting on every resize would throw away wherever the practitioner had panned the moment the panel changed size or went full screen."
